    "result_text": "I've implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`, and it meets all four requirements. The existing test passes (`pytest -q`: 1 passed), and a quick manual check confirmed the retry logging.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Timeouts:** `httpx.Timeout(30.0, connect=5.0)` is set on both the OpenAI client and the HTTP client. The OpenAI client applies its own timeout to every request, so setting it only on the HTTP client wouldn't have been enough.\n- **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n- **Logging:** the HTTP client (openai's `DefaultHttpxClient`) has a request event hook that logs `\"<METHOD> <URL>\"` at INFO on the `app.http` logger. The hook runs on every send, so each retry gets its own log line.\n- **Transport:** `transport` is passed through to the HTTP client. When it's `None`, httpx uses its default.\n\n**Check:** I ran a stub transport that returns a 500 once and then a 200. Two `INFO:app.http:GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models` lines were logged (the first try and the retry). Both clients reported `Timeout(connect=5.0, read=30.0, write=30.0, pool=30.0)` and `max_retries` was 2.\n\n**Two things to know:**\n- **Docs lookup:** Context7 returned \"Monthly quota exceeded\", so I couldn't check the API there as CLAUDE.md asks. I checked the installed `openai` 2.44.0 and `httpx` source in `.venv` instead. No dependencies were added or changed.\n- **Leftover file:** I couldn't delete my temporary check script, `smoke_check.py`, because permission to remove it was denied. Please delete it from the project root."
